  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "At the north sits a huge grassland the novel names Northern Plains.",
      "chapters": [
        334
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan’s arrival chapter is titled for stepping into it, and he confirms he has reached northern plains the moment he stands on the grass.",
      "chapters": [
        426
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The social unit a reader meets first is the tribe. Ge Yao names herself as Ge tribe’s tribe leader’s daughter, speaks of Man tribe marriage pressure, and tells an outsider that without marrying into a tribe others will not take him as one of their own.",
      "chapters": [
        427
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "tribes-on-the-grassland",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_ge_yao",
        "fac_ge_tribe",
        "fac_man_tribe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Yu Tian is a famous Northern Plains pastureland where tribes gather under their banners for a heroes assembly. Liu tribe and Hei tribe stand as the two strongest sides there.",
      "chapters": [
        497
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "tribes-on-the-grassland",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_yu_tian",
        "fac_liu_tribe",
        "fac_hei_tribe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Huang Jin family is the collective name for the bloodlines Giant Sun Immortal Venerable passed on, and that family holds supreme authority in Northern Plains.",
      "chapters": [
        497
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "tribes-on-the-grassland",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_huang_jin_bloodline",
        "char_giant_sun_immortal_venerable"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan uses Ge tribe as a stepping board into the region, and that stretch already treats tribe custom as distinct from Southern Border clan practice.",
      "chapters": [
        439
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "tribe-custom-and-entry",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_southern_border"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Northern Plains’ terrain is flat and boundless. Its tribes move the most of the five regions and are the most battle-hardened.",
      "chapters": [
        819
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "character-of-the-region",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
